aiser.com/disputed-claim-services/umpire-appointment-services/"}}]},"knowsAbout":["Insurance appraisal","California Insurance Code §2071","Wildfire claims","Smoke damage","Xactimate estimating","Umpire services"],"priceRange":"$$","openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"California Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#webpage","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/","name":"Insurance Appraisal Process in California | 8 Steps","description":"The insurance appraisal process in California step by step: the written demand, 20-day appraiser window, umpire selection and the award.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-16","breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#breadcrumb"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#primaryimage"},"image":{"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#primaryimage"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#howto"}},{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#primaryimage","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/clipboard.webp","contentUrl":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/clipboard.webp","width":960,"height":640,"caption":"Signed document on a clipboard beside a pen and camera"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"The appraisal process","item":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/"}],"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"HowTo","name":"How the insurance appraisal process works in California","description":"The eight stages of a California property insurance appraisal under the standard appraisal clause.","totalTime":"P90D","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"Confirm the dispute is about amount","text":"Appraisal resolves the value of a covered loss. Get the carrier’s full estimate and its coverage position in writing.","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#main"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Build your own number","text":"An independent, itemized estimate is the foundation of every appraisal. Without one, there is nothing to compare.","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#main"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Send the written demand","text":"Either side can demand appraisal in writing. Name the claim, the disputed items and your appraiser.","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#main"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Name appraisers within 20 days","text":"Under the standard California wording, each side names a competent and disinterested appraiser within 20 days of the demand.","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#main"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"Seat the umpire","text":"The appraisers have 15 days to agree on an umpire. If they can’t, either side may ask a judge to appoint one.","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#main"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"Appraise item by item","text":"The appraisers inspect, compare estimates and agree where they can, stating actual cash value and loss for each item.","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#main"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":7,"name":"Submit only the differences","text":"Items the appraisers can’t agree on go to the umpire, who reviews both positions.","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#main"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":8,"name":"File the award","text":"A written, itemized award signed by any two of the three sets the amount of loss. Payment follows under the policy terms.","url":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#main"}],"@id":"https://californiainsuranceappraiser.com/the-appraisal-process/#howto"}]}</script>
